  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1247 AM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will shift farther westward Friday into\nSaturday and will be centered over the Desert Southwest. This \nwill result in northerly flow aloft developing over the Plains\nthis weekend, with a weak cold front dropping south across north\nTexas late Friday night and across the forecast area on Saturday. \nAhead of the front, temperatures will be hot again Friday, with\nheat indices nearing 105 degrees once again across the northern  \nBig Country. On Saturday, temperatures will be a bit cooler \nbehind the front, with highs mainly in the mid and upper 90s.\nLow rain chances 20-30%) will remain in the forecast on Saturday,\nas a few showers and thunderstorms will be possible along the \nfront. Dry conditions are expected on Sunday, with high \ntemperatures remaining in the mid to upper 90s. \n\nThe upper ridge will remain west of the area into early next \nweek. Dry conditions will continue, with temperatures warming a \nbit through the period, with highs from the mid 90s to near 100 \ndegrees.",
